config.netherupdatebackport.stone.enabled=Enabled
config.netherupdatebackport.stone.enabled.tooltip=Blackstone and basalt and everything made from them. Off, nothing is registered.
config.netherupdatebackport.stone.generate=Generate
config.netherupdatebackport.stone.generate.tooltip=Blackstone generates in blobs in the nether, in newly generated chunks.
config.netherupdatebackport.stone.basaltGenerator=Basalt generator
config.netherupdatebackport.stone.basaltGenerator.tooltip=Lava over soul soil next to blue ice turns into basalt.
config.netherupdatebackport.blocks.enabled=Enabled
config.netherupdatebackport.blocks.enabled.tooltip=The smaller 1.16 blocks. Off, nothing is registered.
config.netherupdatebackport.blocks.generateGold=Generate gold
config.netherupdatebackport.blocks.generateGold.tooltip=Nether gold ore generates in the nether, in newly generated chunks.
config.netherupdatebackport.fungus.enabled=Enabled
config.netherupdatebackport.fungus.enabled.tooltip=The crimson and warped plants and woods. Off, nothing is registered.
config.netherupdatebackport.soul.enabled=Enabled
config.netherupdatebackport.soul.enabled.tooltip=Soul soil, soul fire and its light sources, and Soul Speed. Off, nothing is registered.
config.netherupdatebackport.soul.soulFire=Soul fire
config.netherupdatebackport.soul.soulFire.tooltip=Fire lit on soul sand or soul soil burns as soul fire: blue, light 10, 2 damage, never spreading.
config.netherupdatebackport.soul.campfireEnabled=Campfire enabled
config.netherupdatebackport.soul.campfireEnabled.tooltip=The soul campfire. Off, it is not registered.
config.netherupdatebackport.soul.campfireCookTime=Campfire cook time
config.netherupdatebackport.soul.campfireCookTime.tooltip=How long one item takes to cook on a soul campfire, in ticks. 1.16's is 600 (30 seconds).
config.netherupdatebackport.soul.campfireExtraFoods=Campfire extra foods
config.netherupdatebackport.soul.campfireExtraFoods.tooltip=What the soul campfire cooks besides food a furnace cooks into food, as 'modid:item' or 'modid:item=modid:result', with ':meta' to pick one variant. Not read when the campfire's own mod is installed: the soul campfire then cooks exactly what that campfire cooks.
config.netherupdatebackport.soul.campfireExcludedFoods=Campfire excluded foods
config.netherupdatebackport.soul.campfireExcludedFoods.tooltip=Items the soul campfire refuses, as 'modid:item' or 'modid:item:meta'.
config.netherupdatebackport.netherite.enabled=Enabled
config.netherupdatebackport.netherite.enabled.tooltip=Netherite and ancient debris. Off, nothing is registered.
config.netherupdatebackport.netherite.generate=Generate
config.netherupdatebackport.netherite.generate.tooltip=Ancient debris generates in the nether, in newly generated chunks.
config.netherupdatebackport.hoglins.enabled=Enabled
config.netherupdatebackport.hoglins.enabled.tooltip=Hoglins and zoglins. Off, nothing is registered.
config.netherupdatebackport.piglins.enabled=Enabled
config.netherupdatebackport.piglins.enabled.tooltip=Piglins and piglin brutes. Off, nothing is registered.
config.netherupdatebackport.piglins.spawn=Spawn
config.netherupdatebackport.piglins.spawn.tooltip=Piglins spawn in the nether wastes, as in 1.16. Brutes spawn only in bastions.
config.netherupdatebackport.striders.enabled=Enabled
config.netherupdatebackport.striders.enabled.tooltip=Striders and the warped fungus on a stick. Off, nothing is registered.
config.netherupdatebackport.striders.spawn=Spawn
config.netherupdatebackport.striders.spawn.tooltip=Striders spawn on lava across the nether, as in 1.16.
config.netherupdatebackport.mobs.enabled=Enabled
config.netherupdatebackport.mobs.enabled.tooltip=1.16's changes to existing mobs.
config.netherupdatebackport.music.enabled=Enabled
config.netherupdatebackport.music.enabled.tooltip=The Pigstep disc and 1.16's nether music and sounds. Off, nothing is registered.
config.netherupdatebackport.music.pigstepInFortresses=Pigstep in fortresses
config.netherupdatebackport.music.pigstepInFortresses.tooltip=Pigstep can also be found in nether fortress chests (the chance a bastion's chests have, 5 in 89). 1.16 has it in bastions only; turn this on if bastions are off.
config.netherupdatebackport.music.biomeMusic=Biome music
config.netherupdatebackport.music.biomeMusic.tooltip=1.16's music: each nether biome has its own tracks, and music no longer stops when you switch game modes or walk into another biome. Client only.
config.netherupdatebackport.music.biomeAmbience=Biome ambience
config.netherupdatebackport.music.biomeAmbience.tooltip=1.16's nether ambience: each nether biome's sound loop, mood sounds and additions. Client only.
config.netherupdatebackport.changes.enabled=Enabled
config.netherupdatebackport.changes.enabled.tooltip=Smaller 1.16 changes to existing blocks and items.
config.netherupdatebackport.changes.hoes=Hoes
config.netherupdatebackport.changes.hoes.tooltip=Hoes are the tool for leaves, hay bales, wart blocks, sponges, dried kelp blocks, targets and shroomlights, and break them faster. Like other tools, a hoe then wears 1 durability per block it breaks and 2 per hit.
config.netherupdatebackport.changes.lavaFog=Lava fog
config.netherupdatebackport.changes.lavaFog.tooltip=In lava you see 5 blocks with Fire Resistance and 1 without.
config.netherupdatebackport.biomes.enabled=Enabled
config.netherupdatebackport.biomes.enabled.tooltip=The crimson forest, warped forest, soul sand valley and basalt deltas, in nether chunks generated from now on, laid out as in 1.16 for the world's seed. Chunks generated before stay nether wastes. Off, nothing is registered.
config.netherupdatebackport.biomes.weights=Weights
config.netherupdatebackport.biomes.weights.tooltip=How much room each nether biome takes, as 'biome=number': 1 is 1.16's (and keeps the map the same as 1.16's for the seed), more grows a biome, less shrinks it, 0 removes it. Biomes are nether_wastes, crimson_forest, warped_forest, soul_sand_valley and basalt_deltas.
config.netherupdatebackport.biomes.overrideOtherMods=Override other mods
config.netherupdatebackport.biomes.overrideOtherMods.tooltip=When another mod has already replaced the nether (with biomes of its own), the 1.16 biomes step aside. On, they replace that mod's nether instead.
config.netherupdatebackport.structures.enabled=Enabled
config.netherupdatebackport.structures.enabled.tooltip=Bastion remnants, ruined portals and nether fossils in chunks generated from now on, where 1.16 puts them for the world's seed. Off, none of them generate and nether fortresses stay where 1.12.2 puts them.
config.netherupdatebackport.structures.bastions=Bastions
config.netherupdatebackport.structures.bastions.tooltip=Bastion remnants in the nether. As in 1.16 they take nether fortress slots: each spot of the grid has a bastion or a fortress, so fortresses move to 1.16's places. Off, fortresses stay where 1.12.2 puts them.
config.netherupdatebackport.structures.ruinedPortals=Ruined portals
config.netherupdatebackport.structures.ruinedPortals.tooltip=Ruined portals in the overworld and the nether.
config.netherupdatebackport.structures.netherFossils=Nether fossils
config.netherupdatebackport.structures.netherFossils.tooltip=Nether fossils in soul sand valleys (needs the nether biomes).
config.netherupdatebackport.compat.duplicates=Duplicate Blocks
config.netherupdatebackport.compat.duplicates.tooltip=When another installed mod adds the same 1.16 blocks and items: OURS hides the other mod's, THEIRS hides ours, BOTH hides nothing. Only the visible ancient debris generates.
config.netherupdatebackport.compat.convertRemoved=Convert when removed
config.netherupdatebackport.compat.convertRemoved.tooltip=Convert blocks and items left behind by another mod that added them, when that mod is removed from a world.
